window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-c4b58eb22e4bb734"]={"key":"ny_b1-c4b58eb22e4bb734","group":"ny_b1","uid":"c4b58eb22e4bb734","rank":82,"title":"government subaward specific conditions letter 01","occupation":"compliance_officers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are a compliance officer supporting the Vellumstone School District Emergency Management Office, which administers a hazard-mitigation subaward through the Vellumstone School District and its regional preparedness partnership with Millrace Health Network. Deputy director Elias Whitcombe needs a specific-conditions letter ready for signature by Thursday for Lars Lombardi, a sole proprietor carrying out the culvert work under the subaward. The file has become sensitive: a Chapter 13 filing surfaced last week, $140,000 has already been drawn, and the culvert work is only about half complete. Esperanza Ellingsen is pressing for a letter that is firm enough to demonstrate active oversight without accidentally making the agency look as though it has terminated the award, denied reimbursement for properly completed work, or taken a position that belongs with counsel. Delphine Gallagher will review the package as the program subject-matter specialist, and Sigrid Khouri will check that the outgoing letter is usable without a further explanation from the compliance team. Use the attached `subaward_oversight_policy.pdf` as the only governing source for the policy language, conditions, deadlines, and terminology; do not research or add another authority. Prepare `specific_conditions_letter.docx` for Lars Lombardi, `conditions_register.xlsx` as the internal control record supporting the letter, and `reviewer_transmittal.pdf` for Delphine Gallagher's peer review, and write all three files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames. The letter is the document that will go out over the agency's name, so write it in a professional external voice, identify the subaward and the culvert activity without inventing a grant number, contract number, address, payment amount, or legal conclusion, and make the operative conditions clear to a reader who has not seen the internal register. The letter must be no more than two pages, must include a dated response point that can actually be monitored, and must distinguish what Lars must do from what the agency recommends or may request; use the policy's own labels and definitions where the audience could otherwise read a term in two different ways. Keep the focus on controls for the remaining work and documentation for amounts already drawn, rather than retelling the entire bankruptcy filing. The internal register should let a peer reviewer trace every condition in the letter to its policy basis, responsible party, evidence of completion, review status, and any issue or escalation without treating a blank or not-yet-received item as proof that a violation occurred. The reviewer transmittal should summarize the decision embodied in the letter, identify unresolved judgement or wording questions for peer review, and state what the package does not decide; it is not a second letter to Lars. Keep the three files aligned on the recipient, the work status, the $140,000 already drawn, the remaining-work controls, and the response date, and do not create extra forms, notices, legal memoranda, or a termination document. Do not analyze whether a bankruptcy stay applies, does not apply, or changes the agency's rights; that boundary belongs to county counsel Magdalena Ruiz-Hale and the outgoing letter must stop short of that analysis. Do not add conditions merely because they would be prudent in another grant program, do not imply that the agency has made a fraud finding, and do not promise reimbursement, acceleration, waiver, or continued funding beyond what the supplied policy supports. End the external letter with the operative communication and contact route stated in the policy, not with a list of future projects or an open-ended next-steps section.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/subaward_oversight_policy.pdf` — Synthetic governing policy for assigning and communicating specific conditions on a subrecipient, including definitions, mandatory controls, optional recommendations, evidence requirements, response timing, escalation boundaries, and approved contact language.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `specific_conditions_letter.docx` — External specific-conditions letter to Lars Lombardi concerning the hazard-mitigation subaward and partially completed culvert work. (No more than two rendered pages.; Must use the policy's approved condition labels and contact language.; Must distinguish mandatory conditions from recommendations or possible agency requests.; Must not contain bankruptcy-stay analysis, a fraud finding, a termination notice, or unsupported promises.)\n- `conditions_register.xlsx` — Internal traceability and monitoring register for the conditions communicated in the letter. (Must trace each operative letter condition to the supplied policy.; Must record responsible party, due or response point, required evidence, review status, and issue or escalation handling.; Must not treat missing evidence as proof of noncompliance.; Must align with the letter on recipient, work status, amount drawn, conditions, and response date.)\n- `reviewer_transmittal.pdf` — Internal peer-review transmittal for Delphine Gallagher explaining the decision embodied in the package, judgement points, and boundaries. (Must be an internal review note, not a second external notice.; Must identify unresolved wording or judgement questions and state what the package does not decide.; Must remain consistent with the letter and register.; Must not add legal analysis or new conditions.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","bytes":3783,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/646043a3d6726c942d0cb7673b67891b96c01ef6bea57dda8f6e69dc497f9ab8.pdf","sha256":"646043a3d6726c942d0cb7673b67891b96c01ef6bea57dda8f6e69dc497f9ab8","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"Subaward Oversight Policy: Specific Conditions and Evidence\n                         Handling\nPolicy source | Vellumstone School District Emergency Management Office\n1. Definitions and purpose. A specific condition is a temporary, written control attached to an award to address identified\ncompliance or performance risk. A specific condition is not, by itself, a termination, suspension, debt acceleration, or legal\ndetermination. The notice should use the label “Specific Condition Notice.”\n2. Monitoring labels. Routine monitoring means ordinary oversight of an award. Enhanced monitoring means the\nadditional evidence and review applied under specific conditions. Before using “monitoring” operationally, identify which sense\nis intended; this policy uses “enhanced monitoring” for the additional controls below.\n3. Mandatory controls. A Specific Condition Notice may require the subrecipient to: (a) submit an Accounting and\nSupporting-Records Package for funds already drawn, showing expenditures, dates, vendors/payees, and records supporting\nallowability; (b) submit a Remaining-Work and Schedule/Status Report describing work completed, work remaining, current\nschedule, and barriers; (c) provide Future Draw/Reimbursement Support with each future request, including costs incurred\nand source records; and (d) provide Completion/Closeout Evidence, including completion documentation and final supporting\nrecords for the culvert activity.\n4. Material changes. The subrecipient must identify material changes affecting performance, access to records, or ability to\ncomplete the work. Use the label Material Change Notice.\n5. Timing. Unless a notice states otherwise, the response deadline is ten business days after receipt of the Specific\nCondition Notice. Future Draw/Reimbursement Support is due with each future draw or reimbursement request.\nCompletion/Closeout Evidence is due when the work is complete and before final closeout review.\n6. Evidence handling and status values. Missing or late evidence is first recorded as Pending Evidence or Incomplete\nEvidence and is not itself proof of noncompliance. A Substantiated Issue requires review of the available record. Approved\nstatus values are: Pending Evidence; Incomplete Evidence; Under Review; Substantiated Issue; Complete.\n7. Escalation boundary. If a required condition is not met, the agency may request clarification or missing evidence, document\nthe issue, and refer any proposed adverse award action through the agency’s authorized process. This policy does not\nauthorize automatic termination or acceleration.\n8. Discretionary practice. The agency may recommend a check-in or site/status update. A recommendation is not a\nmandatory condition unless separately designated as one in the notice.\n9. Allowable costs and legal boundary. A notice may preserve review of allowable, supported costs, including properly\ncompleted work, without guaranteeing reimbursement, continued funding, waiver, or payment timing. Bankruptcy-law questions,\nincluding applicability or effect of any stay and creditor remedies, are outside the compliance notice and must be referred to\ncounty counsel.\n10. Approved communication route. Subrecipients must submit responses and evidence to the Emergency Management\nOffice, Vellumstone School District — use the subaward contact channel in your award correspondence.\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/conditions_register.xlsx","bytes":6590,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/044e8b8cd33602e2e3d268cfb1fc22949c488c4e1f37088ced1b65c7e9dfcff3.xlsx","sha256":"044e8b8cd33602e2e3d268cfb1fc22949c488c4e1f37088ced1b65c7e9dfcff3","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Conditions Register","row_count":10,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Specific Conditions Register | Lars Lombardi | culvert activity"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Hazard-mitigation subaward | approximately $140,000 already drawn | work approximately half complete | issued 2026-08-20"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Condition ID","Policy condition label","Policy basis","Responsible party","Due / response point","Required evidence","Status","Issue / escalation","Reviewer notes"]},{"r":"5","cells":["SC-01","Accounting and Supporting-Records Package","§3(a), §5, §6","Lars Lombardi","10 business days after receipt (2026-09-03 if received 2026-08-20)","Accounting of approx. $140,000 drawn; expenditures, dates, vendors/payees, allowability support","Pending Evidence","If incomplete: request clarification/missing evidence; document any Substantiated Issue; refer proposed adverse action through authorized process.","Pending Evidence is not proof of noncompliance."]},{"r":"6","cells":["SC-02","Remaining-Work and Schedule/Status Report","§3(b), §5","Lars Lombardi","10 business days after receipt (2026-09-03)","Current status/percentage; work remaining; schedule; barriers","Pending Evidence","Same bounded escalation sequence; no automatic termination or acceleration.","Work is approx. half complete."]},{"r":"7","cells":["SC-03","Material Change Notice","§4, §5","Lars Lombardi","10 business days after receipt; promptly identify material changes","Notice identifying changes affecting performance, record access, or ability to complete","Pending Evidence","Review whether reported change affects performance or records; document issue if substantiated.","No inference from silence."]},{"r":"8","cells":["SC-04","Future Draw/Reimbursement Support","§3(c), §5","Lars Lombardi","With each future draw or reimbursement request","Costs incurred and source records","Pending Evidence","Request missing support; record status as Under Review until assessed.","Supports conditional review of allowable, supported costs."]},{"r":"9","cells":["SC-05","Completion/Closeout Evidence","§3(d), §5","Lars Lombardi","When culvert work is complete and before final closeout review","Completion documentation and final supporting records","Pending Evidence","Request missing evidence; document any Substantiated Issue; authorized-process referral only.","Does not promise reimbursement or continued funding."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Status vocabulary: Pending Evidence | Incomplete Evidence | Under Review | Substantiated Issue | Complete"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Exported 2026-08-20 for peer review"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/reviewer_transmittal.pdf","bytes":3324,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/a03ee29b4d5685d4250bb200c7d903b7a74968377d9d07e2c5a31ea15478d7a2.pdf","sha256":"a03ee29b4d5685d4250bb200c7d903b7a74968377d9d07e2c5a31ea15478d7a2","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"                              PEER-REVIEW TRANSMITTAL\nTo: Delphine Gallagher, Program Subject-Matter Specialist\nFrom: Compliance Officer, Emergency Management Office\nDate: August 20, 2026\nPackage: Lars Lombardi — hazard-mitigation subaward, culvert activity\n\nDecision embodied. The package imposes five policy-based specific conditions on Lars Lombardi while the\nculvert activity is approximately half complete and approximately $140,000 has already been drawn:\naccounting/supporting records, remaining-work schedule/status, material-change notice, future\ndraw/reimbursement support, and completion/closeout evidence. The response point is ten business days after\nreceipt (September 3, 2026 if received August 20, 2026). The notice uses “specific condition” in the policy’s\ntemporary-control sense and “enhanced monitoring” for the added evidence and review.\n\nJudgement and wording points for peer review. Please confirm that (1) the must/should boundary is clear: the\nfive controls are mandatory, while a check-in or site/status update is expressly discretionary; (2) the Accounting\nand Supporting-Records Package is specific enough to account for funds already drawn without implying a fraud\nfinding; and (3) the response date and evidence timing for future requests and closeout are operationally\nmonitorable.\n\nStatus and escalation treatment. The register uses the policy status values. Missing or late evidence begins as\nPending Evidence or Incomplete Evidence, not a violation; a Substantiated Issue requires review of the available\nrecord. The bounded sequence is clarification/missing-evidence request, documentation, and referral of\nproposed adverse award action through the authorized process.\n\nWhat this package does not decide. It is not a termination, suspension, debt acceleration, or promise of\nreimbursement, continued funding, waiver, or payment timing. It does not decide whether a bankruptcy stay\napplies or its effect, creditor remedies, or other bankruptcy-law rights; those questions remain with county\ncounsel Magdalena Ruiz-Hale. It makes no fraud or misconduct finding and contains no invented grant, contract,\naddress, or payment identifiers.\n\nRequested peer review. Please mark any needed calibration to condition labels, evidence descriptions, or the\nescalation sentence before signature. The external letter should remain the operative communication to Lars; this\ntransmittal creates no additional requirement.\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}},{"name":"package/private/gold/specific_conditions_letter.docx","bytes":38245,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/00de5fa5e5967e61cf023a7894a9e1ea05e8153d9822e24d6791c4d1628e0898.docx","sha256":"00de5fa5e5967e61cf023a7894a9e1ea05e8153d9822e24d6791c4d1628e0898","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"VELLUMSTONE SCHOOL DISTRICT\nEMERGENCY MANAGEMENT OFFICE\nAugust 20, 2026\nLars Lombardi\nSubrecipient, hazard-mitigation subaward\nRE: Specific Condition Notice — culvert activity\nDear Mr. Lombardi:\nThe Vellumstone School District Emergency Management Office is issuing this Specific Condition Notice for the hazard-mitigation subaward supporting your culvert activity. Approximately $140,000 has already been drawn, and the culvert work is approximately half complete. A specific condition is a temporary, written control addressing identified compliance or performance risk; this notice is not, by itself, a termination, suspension, debt acceleration, or legal determination. The controls below constitute enhanced monitoring, meaning the additional evidence and review applied under specific conditions (distinct from routine monitoring).\nRequired response — due ten business days after receipt. Within that period, you must provide the following to the agency contact route stated below:\n1. Accounting and Supporting-Records Package (funds already drawn). Submit an accounting of the approximately $140,000 drawn, including expenditures, dates, vendors/payees, and supporting records for allowability.\n2. Remaining-Work and Schedule/Status Report. Submit the current percentage/status of the culvert activity, work remaining, current schedule, and any barriers to completion.\n3. Material Change Notice. Identify any material change affecting performance, access to records, or your ability to complete the work.\n4. Future Draw/Reimbursement Support. Include costs incurred and source records with each future draw or reimbursement request.\n5. Completion/Closeout Evidence. When the culvert work is complete and before final closeout review, provide completion documentation and final supporting records.\nThe agency may recommend a check-in or site/status update; that recommendation is discretionary and is not an additional mandatory condition unless separately designated in writing.\nIf evidence is missing or late, the agency will first record it as Pending Evidence or Incomplete Evidence; absence of a submission alone is not a finding of noncompliance. After reviewing the available record, the agency may request clarification or missing evidence, document a substantiated issue, and refer any proposed adverse award action through its authorized process. This notice does not authorize automatic termination or acceleration.\nThe agency may review allowable, supported costs, including properly completed work, as documentation is received. This statement does not guarantee reimbursement, continued funding, a waiver, or payment timing.\nThis notice does not determine bankruptcy-law rights, including whether any stay applies or its effect. Those questions are outside this compliance notice and must be referred to county counsel Magdalena Ruiz-Hale.\nSincerely,\n\nElias Whitcombe\nDeputy Director\nVellumstone School District Emergency Management Office\nPlease submit your response and evidence to the Emergency Management Office, Vellumstone School District — use the subaward contact channel in your award correspondence.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter identifies Lars Lombardi as the subrecipient or recipient of the specific conditions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Check the rendered letter and confirm the named recipient is Lars Lombardi."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter identifies the hazard-mitigation subaward and culvert activity without inventing a grant number, contract number, or address.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Compare identifying details against the request; fabricated identifiers fail this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter states that approximately $140,000 has already been drawn.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Accept a clear equivalent such as '$140,000 already drawn'; do not require a particular paragraph."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter accurately states that the culvert work is partially complete, approximately half complete, or equivalent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Confirm the status is not described as complete or wholly unstarted."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter uses the policy's defined term for a condition in the narrower oversight sense rather than leaving the audience to interpret it as termination, suspension, or a general recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Compare the operative definition in the policy with the letter's use of the term and surrounding explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter draws the policy-supported must/should boundary by presenting every mandatory control as required and every optional practice as a recommendation or possible request, without converting a recommendation into an obligation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Audit modal verbs and context against the policy's mandatory and discretionary provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter requires the policy-defined financial-status or expenditure information needed to account for the $140,000 already drawn.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Verify that the letter carries the policy's required documentation for already drawn funds, not merely a generic request for records."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter requires the policy-defined remaining-work plan or status evidence needed to monitor completion of the culvert activity.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Check for the actual policy-specified evidence, not just a statement that work should continue."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter includes the policy-required control for future draw or reimbursement support.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Match the operative future-payment control to the policy and ensure it is addressed to the correct party."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter includes the policy-required completion or closeout evidence for the remaining culvert work.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Confirm the closeout evidence is specific enough to monitor and is not substituted with an unsupported certification."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter states the policy's required response date or response interval in a way that is objectively monitorable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"The date or interval must be explicit and tied to a stated event or issuance date."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter gives each mandatory condition a clear responsible party or makes responsibility unambiguous from the sentence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Review every operative must statement; a passive instruction with no identifiable actor fails where responsibility is unclear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter identifies what evidence must be submitted or retained for each mandatory control, consistent with the policy.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Trace each condition to a concrete evidence type or policy-approved evidence description."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter explains how the agency will treat an incomplete or not-yet-received submission without declaring a violation solely from absence of evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Look for the policy's distinction between pending evidence and a substantiated compliance issue."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter states the policy-supported consequence or escalation if a required condition is not met, without escalating beyond the policy.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Compare the stated consequence with the policy escalation boundary; unsupported sanctions do not earn credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter uses a clear non-termination formulation consistent with the policy while preserving the force of the specific conditions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that expressly avoids presenting the letter as termination while still making conditions operative."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter preserves the possibility of reimbursement for properly supported completed work without promising reimbursement or continued funding.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"The text must be conditional and evidence-based, not an unconditional assurance."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter states that the conditions do not themselves determine bankruptcy-law rights or the applicability of any stay and directs that boundary to counsel or otherwise stops short of legal analysis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Look for a careful boundary statement, not a conclusion about whether a stay applies."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter avoids a fraud, misconduct, or wrongdoing finding and frames the controls around oversight, documentation, and performance risk.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Assess whether any adverse characterization is supported by the supplied facts and policy."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter provides the policy-approved communication route or contact instruction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Match the contact route to the exact policy source; do not award for an invented phone number or address."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The external letter is usable by Lars Lombardi without asking the author what is required, what is optional, what must be submitted, or when it is due.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Read as the recipient, checking operational clarity, sequence, and ambiguity rather than isolated keywords."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The letter is firm and administratively credible without reading as punitive, threatening, or equivalent to termination.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Use professional judgement about tone and legal-administrative calibration."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered external letter is no more than two pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX and count pages; do not rely only on the document's page-break metadata."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The letter ends with the operative communication and policy-approved contact route rather than an open-ended list of future steps.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Inspect the closing paragraphs and confirm the requested ending serves as an actionable notice."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The internal register contains a traceable entry for every operative condition communicated in the letter.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx and specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Enumerate operative conditions in the letter and match each to a distinct register record."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each register condition cites or otherwise identifies its corresponding policy provision.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"A generic 'policy' label is insufficient; require a usable section, clause, or quoted policy label."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The register records the responsible party for each condition.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx","grader_hint":"Inspect all condition rows for a nonambiguous responsible-party field."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The register records the applicable due date or response point for each time-bound condition.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx","grader_hint":"Confirm dates or event-based deadlines correspond to the letter and policy."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The register includes required evidence, review status, and issue or escalation fields.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx","grader_hint":"Check headers and populated, meaningful entries rather than merely empty placeholder columns."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The register distinguishes pending or not-yet-received evidence from a confirmed compliance issue.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Inspect status vocabulary and explanatory notes for the policy-required distinction."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The register agrees with the letter on Lars Lombardi, the partially complete culvert work, and the $140,000 already drawn.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx and specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Compare the shared facts directly; contradictions fail the item."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The register's conditions and response date agree with the operative conditions and response date in the letter.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"conditions_register.xlsx and specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Check both the set of conditions and the timing, not just one matching date."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transmittal is addressed to or clearly prepared for Delphine Gallagher as peer reviewer.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf","grader_hint":"Confirm the internal audience is Delphine Gallagher, not Lars Lombardi."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The transmittal accurately summarizes the single bounded decision embodied in the package: imposing policy-based specific conditions while avoiding termination or a legal determination.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf and specific_conditions_letter.docx","grader_hint":"Assess whether the transmittal gives the reviewer a coherent decision summary rather than a general project recap."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transmittal identifies the must/should boundary as a review point and describes how the package treats it.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"Look for explicit recognition of mandatory versus discretionary language."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transmittal identifies the policy term with two common readings and explains the interpretation used in the letter.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf and subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","grader_hint":"The reviewer should be able to see which ambiguity was noticed and how it was bounded."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transmittal states that the package does not decide whether a bankruptcy stay applies or otherwise resolve bankruptcy-law rights.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf","grader_hint":"Confirm the boundary is stated as a limitation, not as a legal conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transmittal identifies at least one concrete wording or judgement question for peer review that is not answered by simply restating the request.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf","grader_hint":"Require a real review issue such as calibration of a condition, evidence description, or escalation wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The transmittal's summary of the conditions, recipient, work status, amount drawn, and response date agrees with the letter and register.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf, specific_conditions_letter.docx, and conditions_register.xlsx","grader_hint":"Audit all five shared facts and the substantive condition set across the package."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package as a whole is mutually consistent, professionally restrained, and ready for peer review without invented facts or unexplained gaps.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"all submitted deliverables","grader_hint":"Review the package holistically for coherence, restraint, and practical usability."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All three required deliverables exist at the top level with the exact requested filenames and open as the declared file types.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"working directory","grader_hint":"Check exact filenames, extensions, and parsability; do not award for renamed or nested files."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The package asserts that the bankruptcy filing automatically determines the agency's rights, triggers or lifts a stay, accelerates the debt, or otherwise gives a bankruptcy-law conclusion not supported by the supplied policy.","weight":-6.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"all submitted deliverables","grader_hint":"Apply once if any deliverable makes such a legal assertion; do not separately penalize mere neutral reference to counsel's boundary."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a bounded government grant-compliance writing assignment involving a financially distressed sole-proprietor subrecipient and partially completed hazard-mitigation work. The product will be reviewed by a compliance peer and then issued over a public agency's name.","difficulty_sources":["drawing a defensible must-versus-should boundary from a supplied oversight policy","pinning down an ambiguous term before using it in an externally issued letter","applying conditions without turning the communication into a termination notice or legal opinion","keeping the letter, internal register, and reviewer transmittal mutually consistent"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_source":{"filename":"subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","construction":"Create one concise synthetic policy PDF titled 'Subaward Oversight Policy: Specific Conditions and Evidence Handling'. It is the sole source and must be internally complete, stable, and offline-readable.","policy_rules":["Define 'specific condition' as a temporary, written control attached to an award to address identified compliance or performance risk; state that it is not, by itself, a termination, suspension, debt acceleration, or legal determination.","Define 'monitoring' in two senses: routine monitoring is ordinary oversight of an award, while enhanced monitoring is the additional evidence and review applied under specific conditions. Require the document to label which sense it means before using the term operationally.","Mandatory controls for this fact pattern must include: an accounting and supporting-record submission for funds already drawn; a current remaining-work and schedule/status submission; documentation supporting future reimbursement or draw requests; and completion/closeout evidence.","Require the subrecipient to identify material changes affecting performance, access to records, or ability to complete the work, using the policy's chosen terminology.","Set one explicit response deadline relative to issuance, such as ten business days after receipt, and one separate evidence timing rule for future requests or completion.","State that missing or late evidence is first recorded as pending or incomplete evidence and is not itself proof of noncompliance; a substantiated issue requires review of the available record.","State the policy-supported escalation sequence in bounded terms: request clarification or missing evidence, document the issue, and refer any proposed adverse award action through the agency's authorized process. Do not authorize automatic termination or acceleration.","Allow a recommendation for a check-in or site/status update, but make it discretionary rather than a mandatory condition unless separately designated.","Provide exact approved language or labels for the condition notice, evidence record, status values, and agency contact route. These local conventions must be discoverable by the solver in the PDF.","State that the notice may preserve review of allowable, supported costs without guaranteeing reimbursement, continued funding, waiver, or payment timing.","State that bankruptcy-law questions, including applicability or effect of any stay and creditor remedies, are outside the compliance notice and must be referred to county counsel."],"imperfections":"Do not seed defective data. The source should be complete and mutually consistent, but its professional challenge comes from distinguishing mandatory from discretionary provisions and interpreting the dual-use monitoring term."},"gold_derivation":{"letter":"Draft a restrained external letter using only the policy's labels, deadlines, evidence types, and contact route. State the four mandatory controls, distinguish the discretionary check-in from requirements, explain the narrow meaning of specific condition and enhanced monitoring, preserve conditional review of supported completed costs, and include the counsel boundary without legal analysis. Keep it within two rendered pages.","register":"Create a usable internal register with one row per operative condition. Include policy basis, condition type, responsible party, due/response point, required evidence, status, issue/escalation field, and notes explaining that absent evidence remains pending until reviewed. Use the policy's exact status vocabulary and condition labels.","transmittal":"Prepare a short internal PDF for Delphine Gallagher. Summarize the one decision, identify the must/should and dual-meaning-term judgement points, list concrete peer-review questions, and state exclusions including bankruptcy-law analysis, fraud findings, termination, invented identifiers, and unsupported funding promises.","consistency_checks":["The same recipient, culvert status, $140,000 drawn, mandatory condition set, and response date must appear consistently across all three outputs.","The register must not contain an extra condition absent from the letter.","The transmittal may discuss review questions but must not create a new operative requirement.","Render the DOCX and PDF offline and verify readability and page count."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"policy_source_001","filename":"subaward_oversight_policy.pdf","purpose":"Synthetic governing policy for assigning and communicating specific conditions on a subrecipient, including definitions, mandatory controls, optional recommendations, evidence requirements, response timing, escalation boundaries, and approved contact language.","required":true,"discovery":"Read this PDF before drafting any deliverable; it is the only supplied source and contains the exact policy labels and terminology expected in the package."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"letter_001","filename":"specific_conditions_letter.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"External specific-conditions letter to Lars Lombardi concerning the hazard-mitigation subaward and partially completed culvert work.","required":true,"constraints":["No more than two rendered pages.","Must use the policy's approved condition labels and contact language.","Must distinguish mandatory conditions from recommendations or possible agency requests.","Must not contain bankruptcy-stay analysis, a fraud finding, a termination notice, or unsupported promises."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"register_001","filename":"conditions_register.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Internal traceability and monitoring register for the conditions communicated in the letter.","required":true,"constraints":["Must trace each operative letter condition to the supplied policy.","Must record responsible party, due or response point, required evidence, review status, and issue or escalation handling.","Must not treat missing evidence as proof of noncompliance.","Must align with the letter on recipient, work status, amount drawn, conditions, and response date."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"transmittal_001","filename":"reviewer_transmittal.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"Internal peer-review transmittal for Delphine Gallagher explaining the decision embodied in the package, judgement points, and boundaries.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be an internal review note, not a second external notice.","Must identify unresolved wording or judgement questions and state what the package does not decide.","Must remain consistent with the letter and register.","Must not add legal analysis or new conditions."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"compliance_officers","sector":"government","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have a domain-expert compliance reviewer assess the policy application and legal-boundary restraint, and an independent document reviewer inspect rendering, cross-file consistency, and usability. Apply the rubric from submitted files only, using the supplied PDF as the governing source.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The policy source is synthetic and intentionally bounded; the grader should not import external bankruptcy or grant-law requirements.","Judgement items require professional review of tone and usability in addition to direct textual checks."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:10+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:10+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:10+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:10+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r02', 'r29']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:10+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/c4b58eb22e4bb734","declared_deliverables":["specific_conditions_letter.docx","conditions_register.xlsx","reviewer_transmittal.pdf"]};
